Z||000006||BAM-BAM||04-03-2001||12:38 AM||||  The wheels have universal mounting. They will fit a wide variety of lug pattern/spacings. They also come predrilled for 4 and 5 lug applications. These are some that were advertised on E-Bay. I found sites on the net where they retail for $180.00 + each. The set was $498.00. Now for some tires. BTW, I leave on the 13th of April (Friday) for Montana to pick up my 3800SC seriesI. After I return I plan on going throug it with a fine toothed comb. I am installing CWest 3800 headers so I can use my new Borla with a free flow cat (CWest). I will take lots of pics for all to see. I will be getting some vanity plates for the BULLET that read VTECKLA Or VTECKLR. It might be a little boastful, but fun.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 04-03-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 04-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||04-03-2001||07:48 AM||||There pretty sharp but......I think unilug wheels should have a center cover to cover up all those extra holes. Lisas are the same way. Ive never been big on the 'rivet' look, too hard to keep clean and corrosion free. But on the right car they look OK.||||reg||1
Z||000008||1FST2M6||04-03-2001||08:25 AM||||uum they are 4x100 and 4x114.3 i'd take a wheel off your car and make sure they fit before i'd buy tires... in the even they don't fit LET ME KNOW! they will fit my Miata...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>If they do fit... Yokohama A520s, Dunlop W10s and Kumho Estca Supra 712s. all good tires with decent treadwear and not gunn fall apart like the Toyo FZ4s are know to do. (around here anyway) check <A HREF="http://www.tires.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tires.com</A>  for a good price.. they are even close to you!||||reg||1
